NAME
    export - set and export shell variables

SYNOPSIS
    export NAME[=value]...

DESCRIPTION
    Marks each NAME for export and, when '=value' is provided, assigns
    value to NAME in the current shell's variable table. If '=value' is
    omitted and NAME is unset, NAME is created as an empty string and
    marked exported.

    Exported variables are passed into the environment of child programs
    spawned by the shell (such as nano(1)), alongside the shell-provided
    variables DIANASH_ROOT, DIANASH_USER, and DIANASH_SHELL. Plain
    'NAME=value' sets a variable only within the shell without exporting
    it to child programs.

EXAMPLES
    export FOO=bar
    export EDITOR_MODE
    echo $FOO

EXIT STATUS
    0   Always succeeds.

SEE ALSO
    unset(1), source(1), nano(1)
